  "spans": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "nodeId": "n3",
      "text": "You've likely heard this wild (and wildly misinformed) idea in one form or another: we humans only use 10 percent of our brain.",
      "contextBefore": "n topics like neuroscience, insects, and microbes. ViewFull Profile. --- Learn about ourEditorial Policy. | 3 min read Newsletter. Sign up for our email newsletter for the latest science news Sign Up ",
      "contextAfter": " Like a horror movie monster, the myth just won't die. Various scientists and science journalists think they've killed it. But as soon as they start to relax, it comes roaring back. The fact is, this ",
      "start": 610,
      "end": 737,
      "extractSha256": "84aab4d4b619841df144379f978db93f8ef6a7f62e3956199813edd00dddaa41",
      "windowSha256": "963a16a9ad49b63dccbba298fe424fffd495ff1dfdc7ab00131b93fe79ca11d2",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T17:08:44.980Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20210909232934/https://www.discovermagazine.com/mind/the-10-percent-of-your-brain-myth-that-just-wont-die",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "Adding to that mystery is the contention that humans \"only\" employ 10 percent of their brain.",
      "contextBefore": " equations. It's the wellspring of all human feelings, behaviors, experiences as well as the repository of memory and self-awareness. So it's no surprise that the brain remains a mystery unto itself. ",
      "contextAfter": " If only regular folk could tap that other 90 percent, they too could become savants who remember to the twenty-thousandth decimal place or perhaps even have telekinetic powers. --- On supporting scie",
      "start": 638,
      "end": 731,
      "extractSha256": "13210ebd880bbba475a271b51e14bbf790a02b8b0e48a7cb3099c2d224c9208a",
      "windowSha256": "d8e8e5bd489cf20f2dd6cb6d89acdff0e3a62dcb5f85b7a83d409f8a463f3ec2",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T17:08:47.341Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140616024209/https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/do-people-only-use-10-percent-of-their-brains",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "nodeId": "n5",
      "text": "Nearly two-thirds of Americans mistakenly believe that humans use only 10 percent of their brains, according to a new poll on brain health.",
      "contextBefore": " myths and misperceptions abound, including a considerable underestimation of the incidence of brain ailments.\" Busted! Most in US Believe Brain Disease Myths http://www.livescience.com/39923-amer... ",
      "contextAfter": " Do People Only Use 10 Percent Of Their Brains? http://www.scientificamerican.com/art... \"The human brain is complex. Along with performing millions of mundane acts, it composes concertos, issues mani",
      "start": 888,
      "end": 1027,
      "extractSha256": "218c9e432e63340e95b9d6a62b6e2aac6014ecc85985eb77e48feea53ada4749",
      "windowSha256": "13fea5de84172f67a55ffa2768752a6af4f6b91487ebb2ebbb5642ad6fe73df2",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T17:08:47.922Z",
